{
  "id": "space",
  "kind": "thematic",
  "title": "Space",
  "description": "A researched selection of spaceflight and astronomy postage stamps from the collected country catalogs: rockets, satellites, astronauts, probes, observatories, comets, and the planets.",
  "notes": [
    "This is not an exhaustive worldwide checklist. Entries are limited to already-collected country data. Gambia and Grenada coverage is Postage stamps, 2000\u20132002 only. Denmark and Sweden\u2019s collected issues contain no stamps whose subject is spaceflight or astronomy.",
    "Mixed sets keep only the stamps identified as spaceflight or astronomy. China\u2019s 1962 Scientists set keeps the astronomer Ku Shou-chin. Grenada\u2019s 2000 seventeenth-century sheet keeps Newton\u2019s reflecting telescope, Huygens and Saturn, Cassini and Mars, and R\u00f8mer and Jupiter\u2019s moons. The United States Celebrate the Century sheets keep Explorer I, the Moon landing, Star Trek, Pioneer 10, the Space Shuttle, and John Glenn\u2019s return to space.",
    "Celebrate the Century positions follow the published sheet order, checked against Scott suffixes: Explorer I is 3187d, Man Walks on the Moon is 3188c, Star Trek is 3188e, Pioneer 10 is 3189i, the Space Shuttle is 3190a, and John Glenn\u2019s return is 3191h. Those Scott numbers identify which stamp was selected; they are not stored as verified crosswalks.",
    "Star Trek is included as a spaceflight subject. E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial, from the 1980s Celebrate the Century sheet, is not. The Netherlands 2008 zodiac set is included because its stamps depict constellations.",
    "Excluded title matches: Fort Bliss centennial (a rocket vignette on an army-post anniversary), the Jupiter balloon airmail, McQueen\u2019s Jupiter locomotive, Louis Armstrong, the Lockheed Constellation and USS Constellation, Goodnight Moon, Iceland\u2019s geothermal space-heating stamp, International Year of Planet Earth, Taiwan\u2019s moon-shaped fan paintings and Sun Moon Lake, Gambia\u2019s Venus and Adonis and the moth Uranus sloanus, and Sweden\u2019s Pioneer Jubilee and \u201cSpace without Branch\u201d.",
    "Scott numbers are not asserted for these issues. Existing country crosswalks may still attach inferred numbers during consolidation; those are not treated as verified sheet references."
  ],
  "sources": [
    {
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Celebrate_the_Century",
      "purpose": "Sheet order for the United States Celebrate the Century space stamps"
    },
    {
      "url": "https://postalmuseum.si.edu/object/npm_2000.2020.130",
      "purpose": "Man Walks on the Moon is Scott 3188c, third stamp of the 1960s sheet"
    },
    {
      "url": "https://postalmuseum.si.edu/object/npm_2000.2020.192",
      "purpose": "Pioneer 10 is Scott 3189i, ninth stamp of the 1970s sheet"
    },
    {
      "url": "https://www.collectspace.com/resources/stamps_usstampguide.html",
      "purpose": "United States space-exploration issues, including Celebrate the Century suffixes"
    }
  ],
